    "created_at": "2018-06-22T15:09:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-06-22T15:09:33Z",
    "body": "Hi @jogshraddha, WebUSB is enabled by default on Chrome since [61](https://www.chromestatus.com/features#WebUSB). There are a couple of reasons that may be producing this error. The first is that the origin does not have permission to open the USB device. This can happen on Android if the device has revoked access to the USB device. The second reason is that Chrome failed to grab the device handle. If you are still unable to open the device, please file a bug report at https://crbug.com/ with details on how to reproduce the issue. I hope that this helps.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
